01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
Public Enemies is a 2009 American biographical crime drama film directed by Michael
Mann, who co-wrote the screenplay with Ronan Bennett and Ann Biderman.

13
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
It is an adaptation of Bryan Burrough's 2004 non-fiction book Public Enemies:
America's Greatest Crime Wave and the Birth of the FBI, 1933–34.

14
01:33:20,000 --> 01:33:26,000
Set during the Great Depression, the film chronicles the final years of the notorious bank robber John Dillinger (Johnny Depp) as he is pursued by FBI agent Melvin Purvis (Christian Bale), Dillinger's relationship with Billie Frechette (Marion
Cotillard), as well as Purvis' pursuit of Dillinger's associates and fellow criminals John "Red" Hamilton (Jason Clarke), Homer Van Meter (Stephen Dorff), Harry Pierpont (David Wenham), and Baby Face Nelson (Stephen Graham).

15
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
Burrough originally intended to make a television miniseries about the Depression-era crime
wave in the United States, but decided to write a book on the subject instead.

16
01:46:40,000 --> 01:46:46,000
Mann developed the project, and some scenes were filmed on location where they
occurred, though the film is not entirely historically accurate.

17
01:53:20,000 --> 01:53:26,000
Public Enemies premiered in Chicago on June 19, 2009, and was
released on July 1, 2009, by Universal Pictures.

18
02:00:00,000 --> 02:00:06,000
The film received generally positive reviews from critics and grossed
$214.1 million worldwide against an $80–100 million budget.

19
02:06:40,000 --> 02:06:46,000
The film explores themes of escape, gun, gangster, machinegun, horse race.

20
02:13:20,000 --> 02:13:26,000
The tone is emotional.
